   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>The function that gives the height, <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>, in feet of a cannonball <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> seconds after the ball leaves the cannon is graphed below.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Graph with time in seconds on \\(x\\)-axis and distance above ground in feet on \\(y\\)-axis.\" height=\"243\" src=\"exercises/media/7e7c810f1fc87b7b.svg\" width=\"331\"></p>\n<p>What is the point <span data-math=\"(10, 1,600)\">(10, 1,600)</span> and what does it mean in this situation?</p>",
